  "id": "COMPOUND:18725 - PROTEIN:4972",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound 2-[[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]-2H-furan-5-one and the protein LAMA-84, through a series of target interactions. The compound is identified as a target of multiple entities, including the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is itself a target of several compounds, including Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside and (1R,4Ar,7R)-7-Ethenyl-1,4A,7-Trimethyl-3,4,4B,5,6,9,10,10A-Octahydro-2H-Phenanthrene-1-Carboxylic Acid. These entities are all linked to LAMA-84, indicating a possible pathway where the compound may exert its effects through the regulation of the proteasome subunit 14, which in turn may influence LAMA-84.\n\nThe mechanism appears to involve the interaction of the compound with the proteasome regulatory subunit 14, which is a key component in the proteasome degradation machinery. This suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of proteasome activity, potentially affecting the degradation of proteins that are involved in the function of LAMA-84. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and LAMA-84, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same subunit further strengthens the hypothesis that the compound may act through a similar pathway, though the specific molecular interactions require further investigation.",
